      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Working method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mark the full design boundary on the canvas. Mark the four dividing strips: two vertical strips 2 holes wide at holes 57 and 115, and one horizontal strip 2 holes wide at hole 65. Work all dividing strips in black continental stitch first."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Work each stitch panel in turn. Use the dark shade as the primary colour in each panel and the cream as either the background fill or an alternating element. This keeps the overall sampler visually consistent even though each stitch has a different character."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Panel 7 (Algerian eye): switch to the size 22 needle for the eyelet stitches. The finer needle draws the threads through the centre hole cleanly without distorting the canvas grid."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Block the finished sampler by dampening and pressing under a board for two hours. Full pin-blocking is not used here because Panel 8 (Rhodes stitch) has raised elements that would be flattened by pinning."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Lace the blocked sampler over the acid-free mounting board. Frame in a landscape-format picture frame, or hang unframed as a reference piece tacked to a cork board."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
